audio music "res://assets/music/VN music.wav"
[i]You walk up to the gothic looking house, the faint sound of heavy metal gets louder as you approach the door[/i]
[i]You notice the same musical riff being played, stopped, grunts of frustration, and the riff being repeated once again but changed slightly[/i]
[i]There is bat shaped doorbell hanging on the wall[/i]
[i]You press it[/i]
audio "res://assets/sfx/Vampire Doorbell.wav"
[i]With the sound of Bach's Toccata in D Minor, the music stops abruptly. The door opens and bats fly out, almost hitting your face[/i]

MC: “...Trick or trea-”

VAMPIRE: “Who DARES interrupt me in the middle of rehearsal”
VAMPIRE: “I already told you journalists, you cannot rush an album’s PERFECTION”
VAMPIRE: “I do NOT do autographs nor pictures, leave from whence thou came or your blood shall be for forfeit”

[i]He finally stops his rant and looks down[/i]

VAMPIRE: “A child… you must be lost, or perhaps… you’re a fan?“
VAMPIRE: “…No matter, leave me be… my siren calls and she beckons an answer… but I’m not satisfied with it… I must work”


[i]As he motions to close the door, in a low voice you can’t help but comment[/i]

MC: “It needs work alright”

[i]He stops, immediately pivoting back to look down at you piercingly but amused[/i]

VAMPIRE: “…And what do you know of music, child? I was already cold in the flesh by the time I graced the audiences of Bach, Mozart, Beethoven, Tchaikovsky, and more composers than you’ll ever come to know”
VAMPIRE: “I watched the world burn and bandage itself back together as music was forged and guided with the times.”
VAMPIRE: “And you haven’t even seen my final form”

[i]He takes a deep breath, one he doesn’t need to take, but he lives for the drama[/i]

